course: dictionary
lesson: 14349
title: Sound words
level: primary-4
stars: 1
explain: Some words sound like the thing they name. Oink is one of them: say it and you can almost hear a pig. Writers call these words onomatopoeia. «The pig in the mud went oink, oink.» The word copies the sound, so the sound tells you its meaning.
explain: Oink can be a noun, a verb or an interjection. As a noun it names the sound: «We heard an oink from the barn.» As a verb it is what a pig does: «The pig oinked at the farmer.» Words change their endings for time too: oink, oinks, oinked, oinking.
explain: On its own, «Oink!» is an interjection, a short sound with no other words. «"Oink!" laughed Sam, pretending to be a pig.» Look at the words around oink to see which job it is doing in the sentence.
fact: An oink is the grunting sound a pig makes.
fact: To oink is to make that grunting sound.
fact: Words like oink that copy a sound are called onomatopoeia.
fact: «Oink!» can stand alone as an interjection, like a short shout.
fact: Other sound words include «buzz», «moo» and «tick-tock».
exercise: «The pig in the mud went oink, oink.» What is an oink? | A kind of farm gate | A sweet smell from the farm | *A grunting sound a pig makes | A type of hat
exercise: «The pig oinked at the farmer.» What does oinked mean here? | *Made the grunting sound of a pig | Fell fast asleep | Ate all the corn | Ran away very fast
exercise: Which word in this list is a sound word? | Happy | *Oink | Mud | Farm
test: What job does oink do in «Oink!» laughed the piglet? | An adjective | A noun | A verb | *An interjection
test: Which word is the verb in «The pig oinked all morning.»? | morning | *oinked | all | pig
exam: What is oink an example of? | *A word that copies the sound it names | A word with no meaning at all | A word that means very large | A word for a pig's home
